John,

Thank you for being straight with us.  Ellen asked me to say that first
because she means it and because she has had the other kind.

We cannot take sixteen months.

This is the only time we are going to move these machines.  Nine of them come
out of a room with a domestic air conditioner in it and I have been asking for
four years.  If we do it, we do it once, and a term that ends in March 2020
means doing it again in 2021 while I am also standing up whatever we have
bought by then.

Fifty kilowatts we could live with.  We would start there and grow into it.
It is the term.

What I would ask, and Ellen agrees:

    Come back to us when you know about 2020.  You said you have to give
    notice by the end of September.  If you can tell us in the autumn that
    you have the room through 2025, we would want to talk again seriously,
    and we would not go out to the market first.

    We are not going to wait past then.  The Denver place goes up in March
    and I will have made some arrangement by the summer even if it is a bad
    one.

I would rather do this with you than with the two people I have spoken to who
told me what I wanted to hear.  One of them quoted me capacity I am fairly sure
he does not have.  You told me a number you can actually deliver and then told
me why it was smaller than I asked for, which is not a common experience.

That is worth something to us.  It is not worth sixteen months.

Dinesh
